# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Konstantin Stracke et al. (2026). Evaluating mechanical property prediction across material classes using molecular dynamics simulations with universal machine-learned interatomic potentials.
#   Communications Chemistry. doi:10.1038/s42004-026-02057-9  arXiv:2511.22885v1
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2511.22885v1 (sha256 104106db4c630600...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 232 (Application/model instance). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/stracke2026.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: the six pretrained universal MLIPs used in MD (Orb-v3
# conservative-inf-omat, MACE-MP-0a, MACE-MPA-0, MACE-MOF, fairchem OMat and
# ODAC models, the latter two not encoded as runs) and the 13 materials studied. The paper evaluates bulk
# modulus, thermal expansion and decomposition temperature (percentage
# errors, Fig. 3); no energy or force error is reported, so there is no
# BenchmarkResult.

@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
