###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - Only property errors are reported (bulk modulus MAE 43.8% across models from NVT, CTE 76.2%; per-model errors in Fig. 3), none of which is an energy or force accuracy metric of the schema.
# - The two fairchem models (OMat and ODAC; Zenodo 10.5281/zenodo.15587498) are described only as graph transformers ('GT'); their architecture is not named, so they are not encoded as runs.
# - MACE-MOF is a third-party fine-tune (Ref. [21]) whose base model is MACE-MP-0b medium.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/stracke2026.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.
